{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08SH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B$", "MATH_0002": "$A$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nL_{\\mathbf{Z}[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/\\mathbf{Z}}\n\\otimes_{\\mathbf{Z}[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]} \\mathbf{Z} \\to\nL_{\\mathbf{Z}/\\mathbf{Z}} \\to\nL_{\\mathbf{Z}/\\mathbf{Z}[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]}\\to\nL_{\\mathbf{Z}[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/\\mathbf{Z}}\n\\otimes_{\\mathbf{Z}[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]} \\mathbf{Z}[1]\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$L_{\\mathbf{Z}[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Omega_{\\mathbf{Z}[x_1, \\ldots, x_n]/\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0006": "$L_{\\mathbf{Z}/\\mathbf{Z}}$", "MATH_0007": "$D(\\mathbf{Z})$", "MATH_0008": "$L_{B/A}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-triangle}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-cotangent-complex-polynomial-algebra}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-when-zero}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-surjection}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c8af419291d46aef6d048f36473165f5872b4ed5da6224efd99486438b3a00d4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fdd8bd7a9e0c9cfc9133da7fd92d47a57d488daba0f6c23f180c18a062634956", "source_text": "There are several ways to prove this. For example one can explicitly construct\na resolution of <MATH_0001> over <MATH_0002> and compute. We will use (<REF_0001>).\nNamely, consider the distinguished triangle\n<MATH_0003>\nThe complex <MATH_0004>\nis quasi-isomorphic to <MATH_0005> by\nLemma <REF_0002>.\nThe complex <MATH_0006> is zero in <MATH_0007> by\nLemma <REF_0003>.\nThus we see that <MATH_0008> has only one nonzero cohomology group\nwhich is as described in the lemma by Lemma <REF_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9d4845a43e597234e0ad01bf06fa13bab2071a4bfa9d344ce7f4a97d58c5457a", "unit_id": "tag:08SI:proof"}
{"chapter": "cotangent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08SH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0002": "$I$", "MATH_0003": "$L_{B/A}$", "MATH_0004": "$I/I^2[1]$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-mod-regular-sequence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9956dfb5b63c632b5c643cc119374376948f2b1b41d959fadf48b96b6e2c097c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dca47ad2866c48f5faa07648fe3f26248af23831149e877d15df3cd035e70c50", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a surjective ring map whose kernel <MATH_0002> is generated\nby a Koszul-regular sequence (for example a regular sequence).\nThen <MATH_0003> is quasi-isomorphic to <MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3418a67b2b0536f6626856f10d013dbbe85be92dc449df99bf2e496ad2eb7102", "unit_id": "tag:08SJ:statement"}
